{"user": "Considering I am not very skilled at this game, judge and give me an explanation on why this move would work or not work. I will be placing a black piece on G2", "user_ts": "2026-08-26T14:51:36.947242+00:00", "assistant": "G2 is legal, and it **does flip some discs**: mainly **f2** and the diagonal **f3\u2013e4\u2013d5**.\n\nBut I\u2019d be cautious: after you play **g2**, White can likely answer with the **a1 corner**, flipping the diagonal **b2\u2013c3\u2013d4\u2013e5\u2013f6**. A corner is permanent, so that can be much more valuable than the few discs you flip now.\n\nSo: **G2 \u201cworks\u201d short-term, but may fail strategically because it leaves White a corner.** Look for a move that limits White\u2019s corner access/mobility.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-26T14:52:05.924904+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-26T14:52:07.417452+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Common Ground Question": 3, "Metacomment": 2, "Think Aloud": 1}, "confidence": {"Common Ground Question": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"sonnet": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "gpt": ["Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Hint", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Hint", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 1.0